            <ArticleTitle>Incomplete arterial healing 8 years after the implantation of sirolimus-eluting stent. In vivo visualization by optical coherence tomography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>625-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccd.23215</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The time course of complete arterial healing after drug eluting stent implantation is unknown. We present a case of incomplete endothelialization and late stent malapposition identified by optical coherence tomography 8 years after a sirolimus-eluting stent implantation, which was not related with any adverse clinical event.</AbstractText>
